"
I guard the CairoPlugin's patches against changes of Athens (and of the methods the plugin replicates in C): for each guarded method I know the SHA-256 of the sources that were verified to match the plugin (Pharo 12 to 15), normalised (line ends as CR, trimmed). A group is installed only when its guarded methods have one of these sources:

- `#basic`: each patched method's original (a mismatch skips only that method);
- `#shape`, `#text`: every method the shape and text primitives replicate (all or nothing), plus the rule that no subclass of the classes involved overrides one of them (`subclassOverridesOf:`).

The source of a method that is currently a CairoPlugin patch is the recorded original's; a uFFI callout counts as its source stub. The hashes are in `acceptedHashes` (regenerate them with `currentHashes` in each verified Pharo and add the new values: a method may have several accepted sources).
"
Class {
	#name : 'CairoPluginGuards',
	#superclass : 'Object',
	#classVars : [
		'HashCache'
	],
	#category : 'VM-Plugins-Primitives-Cairo',
	#package : 'VM-Plugins-Primitives-Cairo'
}

{ #category : 'hashes' }
CairoPluginGuards class >> acceptedHashes [
	"methodName -> the Set of the accepted SHA-256 (hex) of its normalised source"

	| d pairs |
	d := Dictionary new.
	pairs := self hashPairs.
	1 to: pairs size by: 2 do: [ :i |
		(d at: (pairs at: i) ifAbsentPut: [ Set new ]) add: (pairs at: i + 1) ].
	^ d
]

{ #category : 'checking' }
CairoPluginGuards class >> check: group [
	"Answer the descriptions of the guard failures of group (empty when it may be installed): source mismatches and, for #shape and #text, subclass overrides"

	^ (self mismatchesOf: group) , (group = #basic
		   ifTrue: [ #(  ) ]
		   ifFalse: [ self subclassOverridesOf: group ])
]

{ #category : 'hashes' }
CairoPluginGuards class >> currentHashes [
	"methodName -> the hash of the guarded method of this image (nil when missing): to regenerate #hashPairs"

	| d |
	d := Dictionary new.
	#( #basic #shape #text ) do: [ :g |
		(self entriesOf: g) do: [ :key |
			d at: (self nameOfKey: key) put: ((self methodAt: key) ifNotNil: [ :m |
					 self hashOf: m ]) ] ].
	^ d
]

{ #category : 'entries' }
CairoPluginGuards class >> entriesOf: group [
	"The guarded methods of group, as keys { className. isMeta. selector }"

	group = #basic ifTrue: [
		^ (CairoPluginInstaller specsOf: #basic) collect: [ :spec |
			  CairoPluginInstaller keyOf: spec ] ].
	group = #shape ifTrue: [ ^ self shapeEntries ].
	group = #text ifTrue: [ ^ self textEntries ].
	^ #(  )
]

{ #category : 'hashes' }
CairoPluginGuards class >> hashOf: aMethod [
	"The SHA-256 (hex) of the normalised source of aMethod (of its uFFI source stub for a callout)"

	| m |
	m := aMethod propertyAt: #ffiNonCompiledMethod ifAbsent: [ aMethod ].
	HashCache ifNil: [ HashCache := WeakIdentityKeyDictionary new ].
	^ HashCache at: m ifAbsentPut: [
		  (SHA256 hashMessage: (self normalize: m sourceCode) utf8Encoded) hex ]
]

